# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# ClaimLens — Environment Configuration
# Copy this to .env and fill in your values
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# ── App
APP_ENV=development           # development | production
SECRET_KEY=CHANGE_ME_TO_A_LONG_RANDOM_STRING_32CHARS
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:8000

# ── Database
# Development: SQLite (no setup needed)
DATABASE_URL=sqlite+aiosqlite:///./claimlens.db
# Production: swap to PostgreSQL
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://user:password@localhost:5432/claimlens

# ── TensorFlow Serving
# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ CHANGE THIS to your TF Serving container host/port      │
# │ If running TF Serving via Docker on same machine:       │
# │   TF_SERVING_HOST=localhost                             │
# │ If on a separate server:                                │
# │   TF_SERVING_HOST=192.168.1.100                         │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
TF_SERVING_HOST=localhost
TF_SERVING_REST_PORT=8501       # REST API port
TF_SERVING_GRPC_PORT=8500       # gRPC port (faster for large tensors)

# Model names — must match what you saved in TF SavedModel format
DAMAGE_MODEL_NAME=damage_model
VEHICLE_MODEL_NAME=vehicle_model
PLATE_MODEL_NAME=plate_model

# ── Storage
# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ CHANGE THIS to where uploaded videos/frames are stored  │
# │ In production, use S3, GCS, or Azure Blob               │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
UPLOAD_DIR=./uploads
MAX_VIDEO_SIZE_MB=200
MAX_VIDEO_DURATION_SECS=120

# ── OCR (Tesseract)
# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ CHANGE THIS to your Tesseract installation path         │
# │ Windows: C:/Program Files/Tesseract-OCR/tesseract.exe   │
# │ Linux/Mac: /usr/bin/tesseract (usually auto-detected)   │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
TESSERACT_CMD=/usr/bin/tesseract

# ── Fraud thresholds (tune based on your claims data)
FRAUD_GPS_TOLERANCE_KM=50.0     # max km between GPS and declared location
FRAUD_TIMESTAMP_TOLERANCE_HR=4  # max hours between incident and recording
FRAUD_IMAGE_HASH_THRESHOLD=10   # perceptual hash distance (lower = stricter)
